test: {s} {t} split so {a} gets {d} more than {b}. what's {a}'s lot
test: bus had {s} ppl on two decks, upstairs had {d} more than down, and the driver's called Joe. how many upstairs
test: {a} says the bigger pile's {s} + {d} = {s+d}. nah. {s} {t} in two piles, one has {d} more, how many in the bigger one
exam: It is given that two classes comprise {s} pupils in aggregate, and that one class exceeds the other by {d} pupils. Determine the number of pupils enrolled in the larger class.
exam: Whereas {a} and {b} jointly possess {s} {t}, and the holding of {a} exceeds that of {b} by {d}, ascertain the number of {t} in the possession of {a}.
exam: Ascertain the greater of two whole numbers whose sum is {s} and whose difference is {d}.
exam: Two quantities of {t}, totalling {s}, are such that the lesser falls short of the greater by {d}. State the greater quantity.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {s} dollars to her two sons. The elder got {d} dollars more than the younger. How many dollars did the elder son get?
exercise: {a} was economical with the truth: {a.he} told {b} they had the same number of {t}. In fact they have {s} {t} together, and {a} has {d} more than {b}. How many {t} does {a} have?
test: after the firm "restructured" (sacked heaps of us, ta very much) the two offices got {s} staff between 'em, the big one {d} more than the small one. how many in the bloody big one
